  "step_1": "The decision reason requires calculating the mean of all outcomes of each lottery by summing the outcomes (ignoring probabilities) and dividing by the number of distinct outcomes. For Lottery A, the outcomes are -6000, 0 (two outcomes). The mean is (-6000 + 0) / 2 = -3000. For Lottery B, the outcomes are -4000, -2000, 0 (three outcomes). The mean is (-4000 + -2000 + 0) / 3 = -2000. According to the decision reason, Lottery B has a higher mean outcome (-2000 > -3000), so it would be preferred. Thus, the decision reason can be applied to the decision problem, and it favors Lottery B.",
